From e6cec45ef8e34e55169fdce99b3ed29644054b39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Peterson <noahbpeterson1997@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:09:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: 32-bit mipsel (GL-SFT1200) support +
 kernel-WireGuard hybrid dataplane

Everything to build and run on 32-bit `mipsel-unknown-linux-musl` (the GL-SFT1200
router), plus the kernel-WireGuard hybrid data path that makes Tailscale
performant on a weak MIPS CPU.

Portability (makes it compile on 32-bit):
- ts_metrics: route `AtomicU64` through `portable-atomic`. 32-bit mipsel has no
  native 64-bit atomic instructions (`core::sync::atomic` lacks `AtomicU64`); the
  `fallback` feature synthesizes it via a lock over the native pointer-width CAS.

Kernel-WireGuard hybrid data plane (feature `kernel-wg`, OFF by default, WIP):
- `ts_runtime/kernel_wg.rs` + a dataplane seam: mirror peers that have a DIRECT
  underlay endpoint into a kernel wg interface via netlink (`defguard_wireguard_rs`)
  so the kernel does their crypto and sends UDP direct (far cheaper on 32-bit MIPS);
  relay-only peers stay on the userspace `ts_tunnel` + DERP path. Needs root +
  `kmod-wireguard` on-device; validated on-device, not in CI.
- First cut: interface name/key/port via `TS_KERNEL_WG_{IFNAME,KEYFILE,PORT}` env;
  the disco->kernel endpoint feed (seam #2) is not wired yet.

Build recipe + device daemon:
- `scripts/build-mipsel.sh` + `BUILD_MIPSEL.md`: reproducible tier-3 cross-build
  (nightly + `-Z build-std`, musl cross toolchain; `link-self-contained=no` +
  `panic=abort` + a `libunwind`->`libgcc_eh` shim resolve the crt/`-lunwind` linkage).
- `examples/glinet_tsd`: a persistent (non-ephemeral) daemon for the GL-SFT1200
  that publishes a status JSON the GL.iNet ucode app reads (login URL / IP / state).

Also: peer_ping allows plaintext `GET /key` for a self-hosted `http://` control
plane (dev Headscale); no effect on the default https Tailscale control plane.

Signed-off-by: Noah Peterson <noahbpeterson1997@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
